# Angular Guide

Angular 21, **standalone** (no NgModules), **zoneless**, **signals-first**. This file covers project architecture. For code style rules (forms, bindings, pipes, TypeScript strictness) see `angular-style-guide.mdc`.

## Bootstrap & DI

- Bootstrapped via `bootstrapApplication(App, appConfig)` in `main.ts`.
- Always use `inject()` — never constructor parameters.
- Services use `providedIn: 'root'` (singleton).

## Standalone Components

- Do **NOT** set `standalone: true` in `@Component` — it is the default in Angular 21.
- Do **NOT** add `changeDetection` to `@Component` — OnPush is the default.

## Zoneless Change Detection

- `provideZonelessChangeDetection()` is active; Zone.js is absent.
- **Do not use the `async` pipe** — it relies on Zone.js to trigger CD. Convert observables to signals with `toSignal()` at the service or component boundary instead.
- When wrapping third-party async callbacks (e.g. Supabase `onAuthStateChange`), call `NgZone.run()` to schedule updates.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — zoneless safe
readonly tasks = toSignal(this.taskApi.getAll(), { initialValue: [] });

// ❌ BAD — async pipe does not trigger CD without Zone.js
// <li *ngFor="let t of tasks$ | async">
```

## State Management

- Use `signal()` for mutable state, `computed()` for derived values, `effect()` sparingly.
- `TaskStateService` is the canonical pattern: private `signal(initialState)` + public `computed()` selectors.
- RxJS only for HTTP streams and complex async coordination (`switchMap`, `takeUntil`).
- Use `toSignal()` to bridge HTTP Observables into templates — do not `.set()` inside subscribe blocks.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
readonly #state = signal<TaskState>(initialState);
readonly tasks = computed(() => this.#state().tasks);

// ❌ BAD
tasks$ = new BehaviorSubject<Task[]>([]);
```

## Component Architecture

- **Smart / presentational split:** smart components inject services; presentational components receive `input()` and emit `output()`.
- Use `host` metadata for root element classes — no extra wrapping `<div>`.
- Use `input()` and `output()` signal-based functions, not `@Input()` / `@Output()` decorators.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
readonly title = input.required<string>();
readonly saved = output<Task>();

// ❌ BAD
@Input() title!: string;
@Output() saved = new EventEmitter<Task>();
```

## HTTP & API Layer

- All REST calls go through `*ApiService` classes using `HttpClient` — never `fetch()`.
- Base URL lives in `todo/src/app/shared/api-base.ts`; import `API_BASE_URL` from there.
- API services return `Observable<T>`; state services or components convert to signals via `toSignal()`.

## Routing

- Routes defined in `app.routes.ts`; all protected routes use `authGuard`.
- Always use `loadComponent` for feature routes (lazy loading).

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
{ path: 'settings', loadComponent: () => import('./settings/settings.component').then(m => m.SettingsComponent) }
```

## Models

- Shared interfaces in `todo/src/app/models/`. Do not duplicate types that already exist there.
- Prefer `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions and utility types.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS only — no component `styles` arrays. See `design-system.mdc` for palette and conventions.
- Global custom utilities go in `todo/src/styles.css`.
